A useful way to preserve the lecture’s order is to write the workflow as an ordered tuple: $\mathcal{W}
=
(P,\ R,\ V,\ S,\ C,\ D,\ H,\ \mathrm{Share}).$ Here $P$ is the page, $R$ is the Reel creation path, $V$ is the selected video, $S$ is the added sound layer, $C$ is the cover, $D$ is the description, and $H$ is the hashtag set. This notation is deliberately modest. It simply keeps the process from collapsing into the vague instruction post a Reel.

