He then immediately softens any temptation to turn one phrase into a formula. The advice is to experiment with different phrases, questions, and calls to action, and then observe what gets traction. A cautious way to record that testing loop is $D_{n+1}
=
\mathrm{adjust}(D_n;\ \mathrm{observed\ traction}),$ where $D_n$ is the current description style. This is not a platform model. It is a practical iteration rule: try, observe, adjust.

